  message: "P3 REVIEW 2026-11-01 (dev 100b6fbb6e; owner-requested re-check of open P3 items last modified before 2026-10-20; fixtures under ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/p3_review_11012026/iobcat4/). VERDICT: CURRENT. Reviewed 2026-11-01 on dev 100b6fbb6e. rust.yaml:370-380 still has no std::process grant, and test_a_pid_is_not_rowed_by_python_precedent still exists. Fixture env::var then process::exit: the \"never launches a subprocess\" claim is inconclusive (\"could not classify (std::env, std::process)\"). An elixir System.halt fixture is also inconclusive. Correction: python.yaml:1862-1870 grants os completeness: complete with getpid deliberately unrowed. Python's precedent is therefore grant-with-pid-inert, which undercuts the reason rust gives for withholding the grant. MECHANISM: module completeness grant withheld because one export (pid read) has no ruled boundary, so exit calls are unexamined. SHARES MECHANISM WITH: WI-vaduf."  # bc34
